Verify that hunspell can actually load the requested dictionary before
advertising the Linux CLI spell-checker as available, and handle '#'-prefixed
no-suggestion responses from `hunspell -a`. Without this check, hosts with
app-text/hunspell installed but without a matching dictionary (e.g. en_US)
report `system_speller.available = true` while silently treating every word as
spelled correctly.

